ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":158,"prev":160,"next":163,"titles":165,"firmware":44},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":12,"order":13,"path":14,"context":15,"summary":19,"status":20,"firmware":21,"facts":27,"procedures":91,"parameters":114,"related":128,"body":133,"sources":134,"official_url":31,"controls":146},"instrument.preset-browser","Preset browser (find and load sounds)",[5,6,7,8,9,10,11],"presets","preset list","load preset","browse presets","sound browser","patches","categories","instrument",70,"knowledge/manual/units/instrument/preset-browser.md",{"modes":16,"screens":17},[12],[18],"preset browser","`shift + Tn` in instrument mode opens that track's preset browser (`shift + M1` for the selected track). OS 1.1.33 opens it by engine, OS 1.2 by category; a click of `E1` swaps the views. A click of `E2` loads the highlighted preset and returns to `M1`.","current",{"min":22,"changed_in":23,"guide_version":24,"verified_on":26},"1.0.9",[24,25],"1.1.15","1.2.0",null,[28,33,36,41,46,50,54,57,60,63,66,69,73,77,80,84,87],{"id":29,"text":30,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"open","In instrument mode, `shift + Tn` opens the preset browser for track n.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/instrument#view-and-create-preset","official",{"id":34,"text":35,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"factory","The unit ships with factory presets across the engines and the sound categories.",{"id":37,"text":38,"source":39,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":40},"whole-sound","Loading a preset replaces the track's whole sound and copies it into the project, so later changes to the preset file leave existing tracks alone.","docs/research/30-presets-samples.md#42-how-a-project-points-at-a-preset-decoded-xy","community-verified",{"id":11,"text":42,"source":43,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":44,"confidence":45},"On OS 1.1.33 the category view lists bass, drum, keys, lead, organ, pad, pluck and strings, after any preset packs installed on the unit (an installed pack is listed first).","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#26-preset-browser-shift--m1","1.1.33","verified",{"id":47,"text":48,"source":49,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":40},"folders","Top-level folders under presets on the unit's storage show up as categories.","docs/research/30-presets-samples.md#41-what-mtp-shows",{"id":51,"text":52,"source":53,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"deeper-folders","Since OS 1.1.15, user preset folders can be nested more deeply.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.15",{"id":55,"text":56,"source":43,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":44,"confidence":45},"screen","The browser shows the track number over the word preset on the left, the engine list in the middle and that engine's presets on the right, the current preset highlighted.",{"id":58,"text":59,"source":43,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":44,"confidence":45},"views","A click of `E1` swaps between by engine and by category, and a popup names the view for a moment; the highlighted preset stays highlighted in the other view.",{"id":61,"text":62,"source":43,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":44,"confidence":45},"sorting","Presets sort by name, factory and user ones together; moving to another engine or category starts its list from the top with the first preset highlighted, and a list scrolls only as far as the highlight needs.",{"id":64,"text":65,"source":43,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":44,"confidence":45},"footer","With one of your own presets highlighted the footer reads cut, paste, rename and delete over `M1`…`M4`; a factory preset shows none.",{"id":67,"text":68,"source":43,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":44,"confidence":45},"loads-to-m1","Loading leaves the browser for the track's `M1` page, showing the new sound's engine values.",{"id":70,"text":71,"source":72,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":40},"browse-loads","In tutorial videos on OS 1.0.x, turning `E2` loads each preset the moment it is highlighted, so the keyboard plays it with its own sound and octave while you browse; leaving the browser with another key keeps the last one.","docs/research/73-overnight-run.md#log",{"id":74,"text":75,"source":72,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":76},"open-loads-nothing","Opening the browser loads nothing, even when the highlight sits on another preset; a click of `E2` loads the highlighted one and returns to the track's `M1` page.","community",{"id":78,"text":79,"source":72,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":76},"factory-values","A factory preset loads with its own stored values, keyboard octave and sends; asinine arrives with the position, envelope, sends and octave its tutorial (OS 1.0.x) shows, though its wavetable reads buzz there and basic in OS 1.1.21 captures.",{"id":81,"text":82,"source":83,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":40},"bass-octave","Bass presets load at keyboard octave −2; every bass preset in captures of the OS 1.1.21 factory set is stored that way.","docs/research/10-xy-format.md#appendix-d--factory-preset-donor-library-firmware-1121",{"id":85,"text":86,"source":43,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":44,"confidence":45},"shift-m1","On OS 1.1.33, `shift + M1` brings up this browser for the selected track, opening on its current preset in engine view; it is how that firmware changes engine.",{"id":88,"text":89,"source":90,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":26,"confidence":40},"opens-by-category","On OS 1.2 the browser opens by category on a new project (bass, drum, drumline, keys, lead, organ, pad, pluck and strings, after any folders of your own), so choosing an engine takes a click of `E1` to the engine view first. The engine view then lists drumline between drum and epiano.","docs/research/81-os12-tutorial-replay-beginner.md#5-differences-most-noticeable-first-video-seconds-b-behaviour-s-screen-a-sound",[92],{"id":93,"goal":94,"preconditions":95,"steps":97,"result":113,"so